📖 Algorithms Implemented

Bisection Method

* Select an interval containing the root.
* Compute the midpoint.
* Replace the interval with the half containing the root.
* Repeat until the desired accuracy is reached.

⸻

Newton-Raphson Method

* Start with an initial guess.
* Evaluate the function and its derivative.
* Update the approximation.
* Continue until convergence.

⸻

Gauss-Jordan Elimination

* Normalize each pivot row.
* Eliminate all other elements in the pivot column.
* Continue until the matrix is in Reduced Row Echelon Form.
* Read the solution directly.

⸻

Gauss-Seidel Method

* Initialize all unknowns.
* Update each variable using the latest available values.
* Continue iterations until the specified tolerance is satisfied.

⸻

⏱️ Time Complexity

Algorithm	Time Complexity
Bisection Method	O(log((b-a)/ε))
Newton-Raphson Method	O(k)
Gauss-Jordan Elimination	O(n³)
Gauss-Seidel Method	O(k × n²)

Where:

* n = Number of variables
* k = Number of iterations
* ε = Desired accuracy

